target aws eu-west-2 1:1
service api 3:9
  image "a"
  port 8080
  scale 1 to 1
  at image 4:3
service worker 5:9
  image "b"
  port 8080
  scale 1 to 1
  at image 6:3
database db 7:10
  engine postgres <default>
  size small
  at engine 7:16
bucket uploads 8:8
  public false
queue jobs 9:7
  fifo false
load balancer web 10:15
  internal false
  listen 80
  route / -> api
  at listen 11:3
  at send 12:3
relation api connects to db 14:1
relation api connects to worker 15:1
relation api reads uploads 16:1
relation api writes uploads 17:1
relation api reads and writes uploads 18:1
relation api reads jobs 19:1
relation api sends to jobs 20:1
relation worker reads jobs 21:1

diagnostics:
warning: `api connects to db` is already declared on line 14
  --> relations.clowd:23:1
   |
23 | api connects to db
   | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   = help: remove one of them

error: `api` can't relate to itself
  --> relations.clowd:24:1
   |
24 | api connects to api
   | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^

error: only a service can start a relationship; `db` is a database
  --> relations.clowd:25:1
   |
25 | db connects to api
   | ^^
   = help: relationships go from the service: `api connects to db`

error: only a service can start a relationship; `uploads` is a bucket
  --> relations.clowd:26:1
   |
26 | uploads reads db
   | ^^^^^^^

error: only a service can start a relationship; `web` is a load balancer
  --> relations.clowd:27:1
   |
27 | web connects to api
   | ^^^
   = help: route to it with `send / to api` in the load balancer's block

error: `writes` doesn't apply to a queue
  --> relations.clowd:28:5
   |
28 | api writes jobs
   |     ^^^^^^
   = help: to publish to a queue, write `api sends to jobs`

error: `reads and writes` doesn't apply to a queue
  --> relations.clowd:29:5
   |
29 | api reads and writes jobs
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   = help: write `api reads jobs` and `api sends to jobs` on separate lines

error: `connects to` doesn't apply to a queue
  --> relations.clowd:30:5
   |
30 | api connects to jobs
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^
   = help: write `api reads jobs` to consume or `api sends to jobs` to publish

error: `sends to` doesn't apply to a bucket
  --> relations.clowd:31:5
   |
31 | api sends to uploads
   |     ^^^^^^^^
   = help: write `api writes uploads`

error: `connects to` doesn't apply to a bucket
  --> relations.clowd:32:5
   |
32 | api connects to uploads
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^
   = help: say what access it needs: `api reads uploads`, `api writes uploads` or `api reads and writes uploads`

error: `reads` doesn't apply to a database
  --> relations.clowd:33:5
   |
33 | api reads db
   |     ^^^^^
   = help: write `api connects to db`

error: `connects to` doesn't apply to a load balancer
  --> relations.clowd:34:5
   |
34 | api connects to web
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^
   = help: load balancers send traffic to services with `send <path> to <service>`, not the other way round
